<Prose
  title="Privacy Policy — CabSnap"
  description="How CabSnap collects, uses, shares, retains, and deletes information."
  path="/privacy"
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  updated="June 26, 2026"
>
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy explains how CabSnap handles information when you use the CabSnap
    Android app and related services. CabSnap is operated by Nuvol Holdings LLC ("Nuvol,"
    and together with the CabSnap app and services, "CabSnap," "we," "us," or "our"), a
    New Jersey limited liability company located at 426 Main St. #166, Spotswood, NJ 08884.
  </p>
  <p>Privacy contact: <a href="mailto:privacy@getcabsnap.com">privacy@getcabsnap.com</a></p>

  <h2>1. What CabSnap Does</h2>
  <p>
    CabSnap helps drivers capture, organize, sync, and export receipt records. Depending on
    your plan and settings, CabSnap may store receipts only on your device, sync redacted
    receipt copies to the cloud, use AI to extract receipt fields, or back up original
    receipt images if you explicitly turn that feature on.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Account information.</strong> Email address, first name, last name,
    authentication session data, password reset state, referral code information, legal
    acceptance records, and account deletion records.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Receipt information.</strong> Receipt photos you capture or import, manually
    entered or AI-extracted fields such as merchant, date, amount, currency, category, and
    notes, receipt deletion status, and sync status.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Redacted receipt images.</strong> CabSnap creates a redacted copy of each receipt
    image after running on-device checks for sensitive payment card details. For Pro and
    Fleet users, the redacted copy may be uploaded to CabSnap cloud storage for sync and AI
    processing.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Original receipt images.</strong> CabSnap also stores an un-redacted original copy
    on the capturing device so you can keep a complete record for tax, reimbursement, or
    audit needs. Original cloud backup is off by default. If you explicitly turn on original
    cloud backup, original images may also be uploaded to private CabSnap cloud storage until
    you turn the feature off, delete the cloud originals, lose Pro access, or delete your
    account.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Subscription and billing information.</strong> Plan tier, Play purchase token,
    product and base plan identifiers, subscription status, renewal status, trial and referral
    credit dates, and billing-event audit records. We do not receive or store your full
    payment card number from Google Play.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Usage, diagnostics, and security information.</strong> AI request timestamps, usage
    counts, rate-limit counters, error details, deletion audit records, and basic device or
    network information needed to operate, protect, and troubleshoot the service.
  </p>

  <h2>3. How We Use Information</h2>
  <p>We use information to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>create and manage your account;</li>
    <li>save, sync, restore, delete, and export receipts;</li>
    <li>process Pro and Fleet receipts with AI;</li>
    <li>enforce receipt limits, subscription access, trials, and referral credits;</li>
    <li>provide account deletion and data export features;</li>
    <li>prevent abuse, enforce rate limits, and secure the service;</li>
    <li>maintain legal, tax, accounting, and operational records;</li>
    <li>communicate with you about support, security, billing, and material changes.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not sell personal information, and we do not share personal information for
    cross-context behavioral advertising. We do not use your receipt images to train
    third-party AI models.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Free, Pro, and Fleet Handling</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Free.</strong> Free receipt records are intended to remain local to your device and
    do not receive cloud receipt sync or AI processing. Account, subscription, legal
    acceptance, support, and security features may still communicate with CabSnap servers.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Pro.</strong> Pro receipts may sync redacted receipt images and receipt fields to
    the cloud and may be processed by AI.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Fleet.</strong> Fleet receipts may be visible to the fleet company or administrator
    according to the Fleet setup. If you use CabSnap through a Fleet, your fleet organization
    may control certain receipt records associated with that Fleet.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Redaction and Sensitive Content</h2>
  <p>
    Before a receipt image is uploaded for sync or AI processing, CabSnap runs on-device
    redaction designed to detect and cover payment card numbers, CVV/CVC codes, and expiration
    dates. Our server also has a safety check that can reject and remove an uploaded image if
    it still appears to contain sensitive payment card data.
  </p>
  <p>
    Redaction is best-effort and is not guaranteed. OCR and image detection can miss sensitive
    data, especially with poor lighting, glare, blur, low contrast, creased paper, unusual card
    formats, handwriting, partial obstruction, skewed photos, or low-resolution images. You are
    responsible for reviewing photos before confirming them and for covering or avoiding
    sensitive information that you do not want processed.
  </p>
  <p>
    Do not intentionally capture or upload payment card numbers, CVV/CVC codes, passwords,
    government IDs, medical information, or other confidential information unless you have the
    right to do so and understand the risk.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Cloud Storage</h2>
  <p>
    CabSnap stores redacted receipt images in a cloud storage bucket used for cross-device
    viewing and sync. The bucket is private and requires authenticated access. When another
    signed-in device needs to display a synced receipt, CabSnap downloads the redacted image
    using that user's authenticated session and stores a local app copy on that device.
  </p>
  <p>
    Original receipt images, when you opt in to original cloud backup, are stored in a private
    cloud bucket and require authenticated access. Original receipt images are not used for AI
    processing.
  </p>

  <h2>7. AI Processing and Service Providers</h2>
  <p>
    For Pro and Fleet features, CabSnap may send redacted receipt images and receipt metadata
    to a third-party AI provider selected by CabSnap to extract receipt fields. Our AI
    providers currently are Anthropic and Google. We may add, change, or remove AI providers,
    and we will update this Privacy Policy if we make a material change to the providers we use.
  </p>
  <p>
    We configure AI processing for receipt extraction and, where available under the provider's
    terms, no-training or limited-retention settings. Provider availability, model selection,
    and data handling terms may change.
  </p>
  <p>
    CabSnap also uses service providers for hosting, authentication, database, storage, billing,
    app distribution, email or support, security, and operational monitoring. Current core
    providers include Supabase and Google Play.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Sharing</h2>
  <p>We may share information:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>with service providers that process information for CabSnap;</li>
    <li>with AI providers for Pro and Fleet receipt extraction;</li>
    <li>with Google Play for subscription purchase verification and billing events;</li>
    <li>with Fleet organizations when your account is covered by or assigned to a Fleet;</li>
    <li>when you direct us to export, download, share, or transfer information;</li>
    <li>to comply with law, legal process, tax, accounting, or security obligations;</li>
    <li>in connection with a merger, acquisition, financing, or sale of assets, with appropriate notice where required.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not sell personal information, and we do not share personal information for
    cross-context behavioral advertising.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Retention and Deletion</h2>
  <p>
    Receipt records and redacted cloud images are kept while your account is active or while
    needed to provide the service. You can delete individual receipts in the app.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you delete your account, CabSnap deletes account-linked receipt rows and receipt storage
    objects from our active systems, signs you out, and wipes local CabSnap receipt data on that
    device after the server confirms deletion. Some records may be retained in anonymized or
    non-identifying form for legal, security, tax, accounting, fraud-prevention, or operational
    audit purposes.
  </p>
  <p>
    Billing and subscription audit records may be retained for up to 7 years where needed for
    tax, accounting, chargeback, or compliance purposes, with direct personal identifiers
    removed or minimized where feasible.
  </p>
  <p>
    AI request logs and diagnostic records are retained only as long as reasonably needed for
    operations, security, troubleshooting, and abuse prevention.
  </p>
  <p>
    Deleting the app from your device may remove local-only receipts that were not exported or
    synced. Export important records before deleting the app, deleting your account, or
    replacing your device.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Your Choices and Rights</h2>
  <p>You can:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>export your CabSnap data from Settings;</li>
    <li>delete individual receipts;</li>
    <li>turn original cloud backup on or off;</li>
    <li>delete cloud-backed original images from Settings;</li>
    <li>delete your account in the app;</li>
    <li>contact us to request access, correction, deletion, restriction, objection, or portability where required by applicable law.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To make a request outside the app, contact
    <a href="mailto:privacy@getcabsnap.com">privacy@getcabsnap.com</a>. We will respond as
    required by applicable law. We will not discriminate against you for exercising a privacy
    right.
  </p>
  <p>
    Some requests may be limited by legal, tax, accounting, security, fraud prevention, or
    Fleet-controller obligations.
  </p>

  <h2>11. U.S. State Privacy Rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, U.S. state privacy laws (including in California, Virginia,
    Colorado, Connecticut, Utah, and other states) may give you rights to know about, access,
    correct, delete, or obtain a portable copy of your personal information, and to appeal a
    denied request. We honor these rights where they apply.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not sell personal information, and we do not "share" personal information for
    cross-context behavioral advertising as those terms are defined under California law. To
    exercise a state privacy right, contact
    <a href="mailto:privacy@getcabsnap.com">privacy@getcabsnap.com</a>. We may need to verify
    your identity before responding, and you may use an authorized agent where the law allows.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Security</h2>
  <p>
    We use HTTPS/TLS in transit, provider-managed encryption at rest, access controls, and
    operational logging. No system is perfectly secure. If you believe your account or data has
    been compromised, contact
    <a href="mailto:security@getcabsnap.com">security@getcabsnap.com</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Children</h2>
  <p>
    CabSnap is not directed to anyone under 18 years old, and you must be at least 18 to create
    an account or use the service. We do not knowingly collect personal information from anyone
    under 18. If we learn that we have collected personal information from someone under 18, we
    will delete it. If you believe a person under 18 has provided us personal information,
    contact <a href="mailto:privacy@getcabsnap.com">privacy@getcabsnap.com</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>14. International Processing</h2>
  <p>
    Your information may be processed in the United States and other countries where we or our
    service providers operate. Those countries may have data protection laws different from
    where you live. Where we transfer information, we use measures required by applicable law.
  </p>

  <h2>15. Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Material changes may be shown in the
    app, and we may require you to accept the updated policy before continuing to use CabSnap.
    The effective date above identifies the current version.
  </p>

